[00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.480]   All information in this presentation is as of the date of the presentation.
[00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.640]   We undertake no obligation to update or revise any forward-looking statement
[00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.620]   as a result of new information, future events, or otherwise,
[00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.140]   except as required by law.
[00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.340]   In addition, today's presentation includes information
[00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.500]   regarding certain non-GAAP financial measures.
[00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.260]   Please see the reconciliations in this presentation
[00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.820]   and the recommendations of non-GAAP financial measures
[00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.880]   attached in today's slide presentation,
[00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.720]   which supplement our IFRS disclosures.
[00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.360]   I would now like to hand the call over to Jean-Marc.
[00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.400]   - Thanks, Ryan.
[00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.160]   Good morning, good afternoon, everyone,
[00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:12.120]   and thank you for your interest in Constellium.
[00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.520]   Let's turn to slide five.
[00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.800]   At Constellium, the health and safety of our employees
[00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.900]   is our first priority.
[00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.200]   We have implemented many initiatives
[00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.140]   to protect our employees in response to the COVID-19 pandemic.
[00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.700]   We have provided our personnel
[00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.800]   with personal protective equipment,
[00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.500]   increased cleaning and sanitation,
[00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.100]   allowed for and enforced social distancing,
[00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.780]   and worked to raise awareness with our employees.
[00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.940]   I want to personally thank our employees
[00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:44.900]   for taking this seriously
[00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.040]   and following the precautions we have put into place.
[00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.780]   As of last Friday, approximately one-half of 1% of our employees
[00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:57.020]   have tested positive for COVID-19, and all of whom,
[00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.100]   have recovered or are recovering.
[00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.580]   Needless to say, we must remain vigilant.
[00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:08.240]   During the second quarter, our plants operated well,
[00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.360]   despite the significant disruptions to customer demand
[00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.060]   from lockdowns in both Europe and the US.
[00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.880]   As I'm speaking, all our plants are running now and well.
[00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.240]   We are carefully monitoring COVID-19 hotspots,
[00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:26.900]   both for the health of our employees and any potential impact
[00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.580]   on supply chains.
[00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.240]   The demand for our products gradually increased
[00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.460]   during the course of the second quarter,
[00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.620]   and this trend has continued into July.
[00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.180]   However, both levels of demand and visibility
[00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.720]   from our customers remain below historical levels.
[00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:49.380]   We took strong actions to combat the effects
[00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.620]   of the pandemic on our business.
[00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.780]   We aggressively reduced our costs,
[00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.780]   including flexing variable costs to match production levels
[00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:01.860]   , reducing fixed costs, and lowering our targeted capital
[00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.460]   expenditures.
[00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.200]   Over 40% of our workforce were on some type of partial
[00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.920]   unemployment or temporary layoff scheme during the quarter.
[00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.000]   Where appropriate, we have also implemented
[00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.780]   permanent headcount reduction.
[00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.540]   Our ability to flex costs was slightly better
[00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.420]   than the scenario we provided last quarter.
[00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:26.660]   This was a great achievement by the entire Constellium team,
[00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.880]   and demonstrated our flexibility and resilience.
[00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.680]   Our liquidity at the end of the quarter was 949 million euros,
[00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:39.800]   an increase of over 300 million euros,
[00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.780]   compared to the end of the first quarter.
[00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.940]   We added an additional 50 million euros of liquidity in July
[00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:51.940]   through credit facilities supported by the German state,
[00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:56.540]   bringing our pro-forma liquidity to approximately 1 billion euros.
[00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:02.820]   In June, we accessed the debt markets to refinance our 2021 bonds.
[00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:06.580]   This transaction removed our only near-term bond maturity
[00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.240]   at a very attractive coupon.
[00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.020]   In conclusion, with the significant actions we have taken,
[00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:19.620]   I am very confident in our ability to navigate through this crisis.
[00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.320]   On slide six, you will see some of our highlights
[00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.820]   from the second quarter of 2020.
[00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.420]   Shipments were 380,000 euros.
[00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:30.660]   In June, we saw a decrease of 10,000 metric tons,
