[00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.300]   Good morning and welcome to Earthstone Energy's second quarter 2020 conference call.
[00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.120]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.520]   A brief question and answer session will follow the formal presentation.
[00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.820]   If anyone should require operator assistance during the conference,
[00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.320]   please press star zero on your telephone keypad.
[00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.040]   As a reminder, this conference is being recorded.
[00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.900]   Joining us today from Earthstone are Robert Anderson,
[00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.820]   President and Chief Executive Officer,
[00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.720]   Mark Lumpkin, Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer,
[00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.560]   and Scott Thielander, Vice President of Finance.
[00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.200]   Mr. Thielander, you may begin.
[00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.140]   Thank you and welcome to our second quarter conference call.
[00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.520]   Before we get started, I would like to remind you that today's call will contain
[00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:51.920]   forward-looking statements within the meaning of Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933 as amended
[00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.660]   and Section 21E of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 as amended.
[00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.980]   Although management believes that the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 as amended,
[00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.940]   these statements are based on reasonable expectations.
[00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.540]   They can give no assurance that they will prove to be correct.
[00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.400]   These statements are subject to certain risks, uncertainties, and assumptions,
[00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.340]   as described in the earnings announcement we released yesterday
[00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:22.140]   and in our 2019 Annual Report on Form 10-K and subsequent quarterly filings.
[00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.800]   These documents can be found in the Investors section of our website,
[00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.960]   www.earthstoneenergy.com.
[00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:36.100]   Should one or more of these risks materialize or should underlying assumptions prove incorrect,
[00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.780]   actual results may vary materially.
[00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:45.240]   This conference call also includes references to certain non-GAAP financial measures,
[00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:51.520]   which include adjusted diluted shares, adjusted EBITDAX, adjusted net income,
[00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.340]   all-in cash costs, cash G&A, and free cash flow.
[00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.940]   Reconciliations of these non-GAAP financial measures include the following.
[00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.540]   The following measures to the most directly comparable measure under GAAP
[00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.480]   are contained in our earnings announcement released yesterday.
[00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:14.260]   Also, please note, information on this call speaks only as of today, August 6, 2020.
[00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.640]   Thus, any time-sensitive information may no longer be accurate
[00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.400]   at the time of any replay or transcript reading.
[00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.520]   A replay of today's call will be available via webcast
[00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.920]   by going to the Investors section of Earthstone's website,
[00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.480]   and also by telephone replay.
[00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.960]   You can find information about how to access those
[00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.040]   on our earnings announcement released yesterday.
[00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.020]   Today's call will begin with comments from Robert Anderson, our CEO,
[00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.040]   followed by remarks from our CFO, Mark Lumpkin,
